# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#on-the-wire
# provenance: PV-0004, PV-0202
# kind: ni-payload
# description: NI_PING\0 followed by one more byte (9 bytes) is not a keep-alive: recognition needs a length of exactly 8.
# derivation: PV-0202 requires the frame length to be exactly 8; this payload is the 8 bytes of PV-0004 plus an arbitrary byte, so rules 1-4 do not match and rule 5 applies.
# expect.class: diag
# expect.reply: none
# expect.reply.frame: none
hex:
4E 49 5F 50 49 4E 47 00                           # N I _ P I N G \0
00                                                # one extra byte (arbitrary)
